  "new_v0_8_claims": [
    "positive affine bounded-profile section operators compose exactly, and the identity affine section fixes every bounded profile",
    "ProfileOrbitHull is the complex-linear span of the full positive-affine orbit of a bounded quasi-polynomial tail profile",
    "ProfileOrbitHull is invariant under every positive affine profile section",
    "ProfileOrbitHull is the absolute smallest linear bounded-profile subspace containing the seed profile and invariant under every positive affine profile section",
    "Fourier-frequency/polynomial-jet coordinates are defined by the ZMod DFT followed by the degree-bounded monomial coefficient basis",
    "ShellJetEnvelope is the smallest shell/jet zero-mask submodule containing a supplied profile submodule",
    "every shell/jet mask and the raw active shell/jet envelope have exact finrank equal to their retained Fourier-frequency/jet coordinate count",
    "InvariantShellJetEnvelope is the smallest shell/jet zero-mask submodule containing H that is invariant under all positive affine profile sections",
    "the full shell/jet mask is admissible, the invariant shell/jet envelope is itself section-invariant, and its exact finrank is its retained coordinate count",
    "OrbitCommonHull retains the full transient prefix and replaces the coarse full tail profile space by the absolute minimal ProfileOrbitHull",
    "every positive affine section, hence every positive-radix depth/address section, of a BellDownstreamInterface sequence belongs to the single OrbitCommonHull",
    "OrbitCommonHull is positive-affine invariant and lies inside the v0.7 CommonHull",
    "under the full-prefix-retention convention, OrbitCommonHull is minimal among positive-affine-invariant sequence submodules containing the original Bell-interface sequence",
    "finrank OrbitCommonHull is bounded by N plus the exact tail-orbit finrank and by N plus the raw active Fourier-frequency/jet coordinate count",
    "if the raw active Fourier-frequency/jet coordinate count is strictly below T(d+1), the refined common hull has a strictly smaller certified finrank bound than the v0.7 coarse bound"
  ],
  "explicit_boundaries": [
    "Bell generalized Cobham theorem remains external and is not formalized",
    "Bell Theorem 1.5 root-of-unity rationality remains checked only in its integer-valued, two-multiplicatively-independent-base regular scope",
    "the rational root-of-unity generating-function to eventual quasi-polynomial normalization remains external",
    "ProfileOrbitHull minimality is inside the declared finite complex bounded-profile category and is not a universal normal-form theorem for arbitrary objects",
    "ShellJetEnvelope is minimal only among shell/jet zero-mask subspaces containing H and is not asserted to be section-invariant",
    "InvariantShellJetEnvelope is minimal among positive-affine-invariant shell/jet zero-mask subspaces containing H; v0.8 does not yet give an explicit combinatorial formula for InvariantShellJetSet",
    "shell-level saturation can be strictly larger than the absolute linear orbit hull because a divisor shell can contain multiple Fourier frequencies",
    "OrbitCommonHull absolute minimality is stated under the explicit convention that the entire N-dimensional transient prefix space is retained",
    "the v0.6 rank/nullity theorem remains restricted to the saved finite complex projector-factorized affine section normal form",
    "the naive base-independent integral normal form remains false and rejected; no such theorem is revived",
    "Lean verification does not establish literature novelty, publication priority, or independent peer review"
  ],
  "external_inputs": [
